Usage:
  nucleus serve [flags]

Start an HTTP server built from configuration only. Modules compiled into your binary are not mounted; to serve your application, run your own binary (go run .).

Flags:
  -config string
    	Path to nucleus config file
  -host string
    	Override host
  -port int
    	Override port
  -without-defaults
    	Serve a core-only app without the default subsystems (admin, authz, mail, storage), matching what an api scaffold's go run . starts

Examples:
  nucleus serve --config nucleus.yml
  nucleus serve --config nucleus.yml --port 9090 --without-defaults
